    {
      "id": "p0085-b009",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "The first problem required back-and-forth testing with the localization programmer to get the timing right. The resulting Japanese scene has Flowey notice the mistake before the word tama (\"bullet\") fully displays. Because the word isn't fully spelled, the letter \"m\" is left dangling at the end, which is what happens after typing \"tam\" with a Japanese keyboard. For Japanese players, this joke conveys a similar sense of \"whoops, that's not the word I meant to use\".",
        "raw": "The first problem required back-and-forth testing with the localization\nprogrammer to get the timing right. The resulting Japanese scene has Flowey\nnotice the mistake before the word tama (\"bullet\") fully displays. Because the\nword isn't fully spelled, the letter \"m\" is left dangling at the end, which is what\nhappens after typing \"tam\" with a Japanese keyboard. For Japanese players,\nthis joke conveys a similar sense of \"whoops, that's not the word I meant to use\".",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.09705254,
          0.49242857,
          0.71242539,
          0.59683571
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.09370907,
          0.49171429,
          0.7144641,
          0.59790714
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          21,
          22,
          23,
          24,
          25,
          26
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "第一个问题需要与本地化程序员反复测试，才能调准时机。最终，日语版里的 Flowey 会在 tama（子弹）显示完整之前发现失误。由于这个词还没拼完，末尾就留着一个 m——使用日语键盘输入 tam 时，正是这样的状态。对日本玩家来说，这个笑话也传达出了类似的感觉：“糟糕，我不是想用这个词。”",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": [
